{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789893600,"nonce":"6A/uMm7BOpZbFCBQQ2NQIuuyKEY=","message":"Fixed in 631db68. Cause: the Cranelift lowering built the value-type table a deopt snapshot boxes registers by (exit_value_types) only when the body had re-tier polls or cold-loop counters. An optimised body with neither — the case when nothing sits above the Cranelift tier, so WLIFT_TIER1=cranelift and 0.1.21 — got an empty table, and a mid-body guard stored every i64/f64/raw-bool register unconverted. Here run(_,_)'s guard at pc 400 fired right after the transfer into the optimised body and restored the integer-typed constants 1, 30, 60 and 7 as denormal Nums, so the next boids[b] raised 'Subscript must be an integer'. The table is now built whenever the body has a guard or slow-path exit. Arena.run at (1000,60), (500,60), (300,20), (1000,5), (200,60) match the interpreter in Cranelift-only, default and LLVM-early modes; benches and the hatch sweep unchanged. The default ladder happened to pass because the LLVM rung gives the Cranelift body polls, which is why it looked like 0.1.22 vs 0.1.21.","files":null}]}